WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.859 --> 00:00:12.580
Ahh, France: the country where the far right
wing, as we know it today, was born.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:14.590
Way before the financial crisis.

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:17.770
Way before Donald Trump became the president
of the US.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:21.160
Way before Brexit, &nbsp;and the uprising of the
xenophobic parties in Europe...

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:28.070
Way way before all of that, France had an
extreme nationalist party, the NATIONAL FRONT,

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.169
and it had real chances to win elections.

00:00:32.169 --> 00:00:37.640
Actually, in 2002 the rest of the political
players in the country, from the center-left

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.340
to the center-right, had to join forces in
order to just keep Jean Marie Le Pen from

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:44.470
becoming the President of France.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:48.579
In April 2017, French people are going back
to the voting stations.

00:00:48.579 --> 00:00:53.420
And a lot of people think that this is the
ultimate chance for the far right wing in

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.420
France.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:59.570
The moment where the NATIONAL FRONT, with
MARINE LE PEN as its leader, can get the presidential

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:01.510
office once for all.

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:04.750
If this was the case, Marine Le Pen, who,
by the way, is the daughter of Jean Marie

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:09.640
Le Pen, has promised she will do everything
she can to take her country out of European

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:10.640
Union.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:11.640
But not only that...

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.900
France is the second largest country in Continental
Europe.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:21.510
A victory of the extreme right would be a
triumph for all far-right parties on the continent.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:25.810
But wait just a minute...

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.460
Because now the question is…

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:32.369
Does Marine Le Pen have a REAL chance of winning
this election?

00:01:32.369 --> 00:01:34.229
Can anyone stop her?

00:01:34.229 --> 00:01:38.670
Today we will answer to all of this questions,
and we’re going to get to know, in-depth,

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:43.970
the history of the French extreme right: a
story that includes family wars, ego clashes

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.049
and… well… playmates.

00:01:46.049 --> 00:01:48.900
So, let’s get into it.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.259
THE LE PEN CLAN

00:01:51.259 --> 00:01:54.830
The French extreme right wing has two ideological
grandparents:

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:57.689
Adolf Hitler and the OAS.

00:01:57.689 --> 00:02:02.670
As you know, during World War II, Germans
invaded the North of France.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:08.310
But the South, the so called “free zone”,
whose capital was the city of VICHY, was governed

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:12.549
by French politicians who supported the German
National Socialism too.

00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:16.620
When the war ended, the new French President,
General Charles de Gaulle, executed the main

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.770
officials from Vichy.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:22.190
But wait a minute, because still, there were
many other people that supported that collaborationist

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:23.190
government.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:26.940
People that, even without having political
power, held the same principles and the same

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:34.520
ideals of the National Socialists from Nazi
Germany.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.270
And many of them were in the army!

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.640
&nbsp;
Decades later, in 1961, the French let their

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.280
most precious colony, Algeria, hold a self-determination
referendum.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:47.080
As you can imagine, this was not good news
for all those far right wing extremist inside

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.080
of the French army.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.870
This is how the OAS was born.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:58.860
The OAS was a terrorist group whose main goal
was to end the Algerian attempt for independence.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:07.690
So, did they succeed?

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:08.690
Actually not.

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:11.599
In 1962, Algeria became a sovereign state.

00:03:11.599 --> 00:03:15.140
And then, the OAS changed their goals and
tried the kill the French President himself!

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:18.970
They thought De Gaulle was a traitor to the
country.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:22.709
Fortunately, in 1965, the French police dismantled
the last cells of this group.

00:03:22.709 --> 00:03:26.160
Just like what happened after the end of the
World War II though, jailing the hardliners

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:31.530
didn’t mean there were no more people supporting
the general cause.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:38.260
France, the country of the liberty, equality
and fraternity, had a large amount of people

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:42.460
who hated the Algerians and had a nostalgia
for the Third Reich.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:48.170
And this was the foundation that JEAN MARIE
LE PEN used to build, 10 years later, the

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:49.170
NATIONAL FRONT.

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:54.459
“It is the media who only talk about the
war, over and over.

00:03:54.459 --> 00:04:00.000
Everyday we are reminded of what the war was:
The persecution of the Jews, the excessive

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.870
behaviour of the occupying forces and so on...”

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:05.260
The beginning of this party was not an easy
thing.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:10.030
During the 1970s, the NATIONAL FRONT would
never get more than a 5% of the vote.

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:13.640
And Marie Le Pen himself suffered a terrorist
attack at his own house.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:17.820
Now this is when the good part starts!

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:27.389
In 1977, the Le Pen family inherited, from
a fellow supporter, an entire palace.

00:04:27.389 --> 00:04:28.530
The Montretout Palace.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:33.999
Soon this would become the unofficial headquarters
of the National Front or… we might as well

00:04:33.999 --> 00:04:35.030
say - the Le Pen family.

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:38.119
&nbsp;
Yes, my friend, with this party, everything

00:04:38.119 --> 00:04:40.139
stays in the family.

00:04:40.139 --> 00:04:46.400
From the Montretout palace, Jean Marie organized
all those electoral campaigns that made him

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:49.960
the third biggest political force in France
at the end of the 80s.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:54.219
Meanwhile, his daughter, Marine Le Pen, was
following him and learning the secrets and

00:04:54.219 --> 00:04:58.860
the art of politics in order to become the
leader she is today.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.360
Later, his granddaughter, MARION LE PEN, would
follow him too.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:05.469
And she is now an MP in the French Parliament
and the rising star of the National Front.

00:05:05.469 --> 00:05:09.749
Interestingly, though, even though his party
congratulates him as the champion of family

00:05:09.749 --> 00:05:10.749
values…

00:05:10.749 --> 00:05:13.080
Le Pen’s family is far from a happy one.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.080
Yes, yes…

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.059
I know, here at VisualPolitik we don’t like
to gossip about the private life of anyone…

00:05:17.059 --> 00:05:24.879
But in this case, it’s absolutely necessary
to understand the political life of this party!

00:05:24.879 --> 00:05:31.460
As I said, in the 1980s, Jean Marie Le Pen,
whom we will call from now on, Le Pen senior,

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:32.770
was on fire.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:36.289
nN every election, he was getting more votes
than the previous one.

00:05:36.289 --> 00:05:41.229
In this moment, he hired a journalist to write
his own biography.

00:05:41.229 --> 00:05:47.639
And, of course, he let him stay at his palace.

00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:51.289
And guess what that journalist did?

00:05:51.289 --> 00:05:54.800
Well, he seduced Le Pen´s wife.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:56.969
Ohhh, but not only that...

00:05:56.969 --> 00:05:59.369
These two lovers ran away from the palace.

00:05:59.369 --> 00:06:03.740
And months later, Mrs. Le Pen was on the cover
of the French Playboy magazine.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:08.509
And this is how the whole world discovered
the… err… more sensual side of the extreme

00:06:08.509 --> 00:06:10.249
right wing.

00:06:10.249 --> 00:06:19.469
PICTURES OF LE PEN IN PLAYBOY.

00:06:19.469 --> 00:06:20.969
This caused a split in the family.

00:06:20.969 --> 00:06:25.349
No matter how good the father was doing in
the elections, his daughter still grew more

00:06:25.349 --> 00:06:26.379
and more distant from him.

00:06:26.379 --> 00:06:30.990
But the real turning point in the Le Pen family
would come in the year 2002.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:34.590
This was a year when France held presidential
elections.

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:38.699
And for the first time in history, Le Pen
went to the second round.

00:06:38.699 --> 00:06:45.059
As you might know, the French electoral system
has two rounds.

00:06:45.059 --> 00:06:49.189
When they are choosing a president, in the
first round they can choose from all the candidates,

00:06:49.189 --> 00:06:50.189
however many that may be.

00:06:50.189 --> 00:06:53.710
After this round, there is a second one where
only one of the two most successful candidates

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:54.710
can be chosen.

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:58.749
Well, in this 2002, the ones who made it the
the second round where Jacques CHIRAC, from

00:06:58.749 --> 00:07:03.719
the center-right wing party, and Le Pen senior,
from the extreme right wing.

00:07:03.719 --> 00:07:09.029
&nbsp;
And now you might wonder…

00:07:09.029 --> 00:07:11.310
How is that possible that they had two right
wing candidates?

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:13.270
Are there no liberals in France?

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:18.539
Well during these years, Le Pen learnt an
important lesson in politics: the idea of

00:07:18.539 --> 00:07:19.979
the “captive voter”.

00:07:19.979 --> 00:07:24.300
A voter that is going to find some principles
of the party attractive, no matter where they

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:25.809
stand on the political spectrum.

00:07:25.809 --> 00:07:29.689
Le Pen stood for protectionism for French
companies, but also for French workers.

00:07:29.689 --> 00:07:32.159
Do you remember the “America first” thing?

00:07:32.159 --> 00:07:34.839
Yep, turns out that’s not Trumps invention.

00:07:34.839 --> 00:07:37.580
It was used by Le Pen in the 1990s.

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:42.199
So in 2002, industrial cities like MARSEILLE,
who used to be the left wing strongholds,

00:07:42.199 --> 00:07:48.979
voted for the National Front.

00:07:48.979 --> 00:07:53.110
And this is why in this second round, those
who remained loyal to the Social democratic

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:58.869
party had to swallow their pride and vote
for Jaques Chirac, the center-right candidate.

00:07:58.869 --> 00:08:05.360
Anything was better than the uprising of a
racist, extreme conservative like Le Pen.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:13.459
And this is how the Le Pen family learned
a second lesson in politics: is not enough

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:15.889
getting accepted by your voters…

00:08:15.889 --> 00:08:18.479
you also cannot be too scary to the others.

00:08:18.479 --> 00:08:22.599
If your opposition are too frightened, they
might join forces to prevent you from getting

00:08:22.599 --> 00:08:25.029
into the Presidential Palace.

00:08:25.029 --> 00:08:27.719
MARINE VS.

00:08:27.719 --> 00:08:29.990
JEAN MARIE VS.

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:30.990
MARION
&nbsp;

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:34.420
Christmas was not a great time for the family
after 2002.

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:37.530
Marine Le Pen started her internal campaign
against her father.

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:42.399
Now, don’t forget that Jean Marie Le Pen
was a politician that ran for elections with

00:08:42.399 --> 00:08:43.849
statements like this one:

00:08:43.849 --> 00:08:50.000
“There has to be an authority, always, and
we believe that, in a household, the best

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.040
one to have this authority is the man.”

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:53.190
–Jean Marie Le Pen (Le droit ajourd´hui,
1979).

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:54.960
&nbsp;
Nonetheless, Marine Le Pen was a woman ready

00:08:54.960 --> 00:09:00.910
to have authority and modernise a political
party that would made Windows 95 look like

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:02.520
state of the art.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:07.470
Unlike her father, Marine supported gay civil
unions and was against death penalty.

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:10.420
Even National Front voters could appreciate
these changes.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:15.319
And this is why, in 2011, Le Pen junior took
her father’s place as the party leader.

00:09:15.319 --> 00:09:18.110
Ahh, but things, they weren’t that easy...

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:24.079
“I wonder what motivated Marine and her
deputies in this offensive they launched against

00:09:24.079 --> 00:09:25.989
me”.

00:09:25.989 --> 00:09:26.989
&nbsp;
Just think about it.

00:09:26.989 --> 00:09:31.650
When you have been the founder and leader
of the French far right for 39 years, it's

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:35.009
not easy to put up with your daughter giving
you orders.

00:09:35.009 --> 00:09:38.980
So, even though today, Jean Marie Le Pen is
the honorary president of the National Front…

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:42.790
he also votes as an independent at the European
Parliament.

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:49.389
“I campaigned not for Marine Le Pen, but
for Jean-Marie Le Pen and I won 33%.”

00:09:49.389 --> 00:09:51.770
And guess who is his main supporter inside
of the party?

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:52.770
Surprise surprise!

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:57.149
Family business again, it’s his granddaughter,
MARION Le Pen, who is starting her own battle

00:09:57.149 --> 00:10:04.290
against her aunt, Marine.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:18.569
“I think that 
Europe has made a mistake in the past.

00:10:18.569 --> 00:10:23.079
They should have started cooperation and development
of relationships with Africa.

00:10:23.079 --> 00:10:26.540
This way they would have fixed the people
in their own countries.”

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:32.389
In fact, the latest pollsters for this 2017
elections give her close to 25% of vote.

00:10:32.389 --> 00:10:35.079
This makes her the first or the second biggest
candidate.

00:10:35.079 --> 00:10:40.089
And in an election with 5 candidates, 25%
is a big thing.

00:10:40.089 --> 00:10:43.649
It is almost certain that she will make it
into the second round.

00:10:43.649 --> 00:10:47.370
But do consider that just because she is less
radical than her father this doesn’t mean

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.940
that Marine is a moderate.

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:56.209
Far from this in fact.

00:10:56.209 --> 00:11:01.300
In her famous 144 points of her electoral
manifesto, Le Pen junior stands for closing

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:06.480
frontiers, massive deportations, the exit
of the European Union, and the return of the

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:08.480
French currency.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:13.170
“I hold the same economic views as Vladimir
Putin.

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:14.370
This is true.

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:16.279
But this is nothing new either.”

00:11:16.279 --> 00:11:18.399
&nbsp;
Alright, enough, now you are probably wondering...

00:11:18.399 --> 00:11:22.129
Well, can Le Pen actually become the new French
President?

00:11:22.129 --> 00:11:25.110
Let’s address this question, with another
question...

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:29.639
WHO CAN STOP LE PEN?

00:11:29.639 --> 00:11:34.290
For years, the center-right wing in France
saw how Le Pen could steal their votes.

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:38.860
Yes, it is true that a big share of the National
Front votes come from the left wing.

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:43.399
But in a this time of crisis, family values
and anti-immigrant sentiments are particularly

00:11:43.399 --> 00:11:45.389
attractive for conservative voters.

00:11:45.389 --> 00:11:51.320
So in 2016, the big party of the center-right,
THE REPUBLICANS, chose a candidate who also

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:55.300
put forward some of the proposals that made
Le Pen famous.

00:11:55.300 --> 00:12:00.319
This man was FRANCOIS FILLON.

00:12:00.319 --> 00:12:05.589
&nbsp;
So, is that strategy working?

00:12:05.589 --> 00:12:07.839
Well… apparently not.

00:12:07.839 --> 00:12:12.170
Since Fillon became the party’s candidate,
Republicans have fallen on the polls and now

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:16.300
they are fighting for third position with
the far-left wing party of Jean Luc Melenchon.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:19.389
Corruption, sex scandals and the fact that
voters prefer the original (Le Pen) to the

00:12:19.389 --> 00:12:24.889
copy, has caused Fillon and the center-right
to fall into oblivion.

00:12:24.889 --> 00:12:27.930
But there is still hope!

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.430
The battle is not over.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:33.069
There is still a man ready to stop Le Pen’s
hurricane.

00:12:33.069 --> 00:12:36.769
His name is EMMANUEL MARCON and he was the
finance minister during the government of

00:12:36.769 --> 00:12:39.770
Manuel VALLS.

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:44.550
Alright, so is Emmanuel Marcon a socialist?

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:45.550
Hell no!

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:48.200
Macron is running in the elections as an independent.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.600
Even Manuel Valls himself didn’t support
him in public until recently.

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:54.370
But what does Emmanuel Macron stand for?

00:12:54.370 --> 00:13:03.620
Basically, just the opposite of Le Pen.

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:07.329
Macron wants to end the privileges and subsidies
that French companies get.

00:13:07.329 --> 00:13:11.060
He wants to end the barriers that made it
impossible for the French to get a job.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:14.620
And, of course, he is against discrimination
based on race or religion.

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:19.120
When it comes to the economy, he wants to
be the champion of deficit reduction and fiscal

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.410
responsibility.

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:25.089
And if this was not enough, one of his proposals
is to forbid high ranking officials to employ

00:13:25.089 --> 00:13:27.600
their own family inside of the administration.

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:31.140
So... as you can see, he is the antithesis
of Marine Le Pen.

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:35.430
And surprise surprise, the latest polls suggest
he is slightly more popular than Marine Le

00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:43.630
Pen - with over 25% of the expected.

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:46.060
And all of this, despite being an independent.

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:53.720
So he has a high chance of being the person
who will face Le Pen in the second round.&nbsp;

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:58.329
Or… maybe not?

00:13:58.329 --> 00:14:03.140
There is a last variable we have to consider:
ABSTENTION.

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:07.680
Even if Macron has a lot of supporters, they
are simply not as motivated as those from

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:08.680
the Le Pen side.

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:13.310
So, for example, if during the second round,
the National Front could retain 90% of their

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:24.129
voters and Macron could only retain 40 or
50%, he would have difficulty winning 

00:14:24.129 --> 00:14:25.129
the presidency.

00:14:25.129 --> 00:14:28.060
But this is our opinion, now we wanna hear
yours.

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:29.879
Can Macron beat Le Pen?

00:14:29.879 --> 00:14:34.480
Could any of the other candidates make a surprise
resurgence during the elections?

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:36.410
Please, leave your answer on the comment section
below, we’d love to hear from you.

